$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,6-Bis(dioctylphosphinoyl)-2,5-dibutyl-2,5-diazahexane (X). A mixture of
8.22 g of dioctylphosphinous acid, 0.9 g of Paraform, and 2.58 g of N,N-
dibutylethylenediamine was refluxed in toluene with removal of water for
3 h. Over the reaction period, 0.25 ml of water was collected. The
toluene was removed in a vacuum, and the residue was heated for 6 h at
145°C to obtain a crude product. Column chromatography gave 8.1 g of a
viscous light yellow liquid. Yield 11 g (99%). nD20: 1.472; Rf: 0.35; IR
spectrum, ν(P=O), cm-1: 1140; δ , ppm: 49; Found, %: C 70.97, H 12.63, P
8.33; Calculated, %: C 70.97, H 12.52, P 8.43; Formula: C44H94N2O2P2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM paraformaldehyde used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and ionophoric properties of α,ω-diphosphorylated aza podands:
II. Kabachnik-fields reaction as a method for design of
α,ω-diphosphorylated aza podands and their use for determination of metal
ions
