$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of [mpIm]Cl A mixture of (3-chloropropyl)triethoxysilane (5
mmol) and 1- methylimidazole (5 mmol) was stirred for 20 h at 80°C under
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixturewas concentrated on a rotary
evaporator under reduced pressure. The desired product44 (viscous oil;
yield: 95%). Synthesis of MWCNT–[mpIm]HSO4 To a stirried solution of
[mpIm]Cl (5 mmol) in 1,2- dichloroethane (20 mL), MWCNT–OH (1 g) was
added and the mixture was refluxed for 20 h under nitrogen atmosphere.
Then, the solid was filtered off, washed with 1,2-dichloroethane (15 mL),
and dried in a vacuum oven at 100°C for 24 h. Afterwards, H2SO4 (10mL,
8M) was added dropwise to the resulting solid at room temperature and
themixture was stirred at 40°C for 48 h, filtered, washed with
distilledwater (20mL) and dried at 100°C overnight. MWCNT–[mpIm]HSO4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of α-aminophosphonates using carbon nanotube supported
imidazolium salt-based ionic liquid as a novel and environmentally benign
catalyst
