$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl (diethoxymethyl)-H-phosphinate (Ciba-Geigy reagent) 29a (Scheme
3).5 To a solution of concentrated H3PO2 (20 g, 303 mmol) was added
slowly, at room temperature under nitrogen, trifluoroacetic acid (6.9 g,
60.6 mmol, 4.7 mL) then triethylorthoformate (98.8 g, 667 mmol, 111 mL).
After 4 h of stirring at room temperature, chloroform was added (200 mL)
and a solution of saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (exothermic reaction) was
added. The organic layer was extracted. Drying and concentration afforded
the product as a yellow oil (55.8 g, 94%). Ethyl
(diethoxymethyl)-H-phosphinate (Ciba-Geigy reagent) 29a, Yield (55.8 g,
94%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 5.75-5.95 (m, 1H), 5.18 (d, J= 17 Hz,
1H), 5.09 (d, J= 10 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (q, J= 14 Hz, J= 7 Hz, 2H), 3.70-3.81
(m, 2H), 1.24 (t, J= 7 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.45 MHz) δ 156.8,
134.9, 115.8, 60.8, 43.4, 14.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of P,N-heterocycles from ω-amino-H-phosphinates:
conformationally restricted α-amino acid analogs
