$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [2-(1,3-dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-yl)-ethyl]-H-phosphinic acid ethyl
ester 34 (Scheme 4).7 To (2-phthalimidoethyl)phosphinic acid 11 (5 g, 21
mmol) in toluene (75 mL) was added tetra-n-ethyl orthosilicate (4.37 g,
21 mmol) under N2 and the mixture was refluxed for 24 h. The solvent
removed by vacuo and the resulting oil was purified by column
chromatography (silica, EtOAc 100%) to afford the desired product 34 as a
white solid (5.2 g, 93%).
[2-(1,3-dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-yl)-ethyl]-H-phosphinic acid ethyl
ester 34, Yield (5.2 g, 93%). mp 52-54 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ
7.70-7.90 (m, 4H),7.24 (d, J= 542 Hz, 1H), 3.90-4.25 (m, 4H), 2.20-2.35
(m, 2H), 1.28 (t, J= 7 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.45 MHz) δ 168.0 (2C),
134.4 (2C), 132.1 (2C), 123.6 (2C), 63.1 (d, JPOC = 7 Hz ), 30.7, 28.3
(d, JPCN = 92 Hz), 16.3 (d, JPOCC = 7 Hz ); 31P NMR (CDCl3, 121.47 MHz) δ
34.5 (dm, J= 542 Hz); HRMS (EI+) calc for C12H14NO4P 267.0660, found
267.0655.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of P,N-heterocycles from ω-amino-H-phosphinates:
conformationally restricted α-amino acid analogs
