$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: α -Aminophosphonates 4; General Procedure The
amine 2 (2.2 mmol) and aldehyde 1 (2 mmol) were stirred for a few minutes
at r.t. in MeCN (4 mL) before the P(OMe)3 (3; 2.2 mmol) and Amberlyst-15
(0.2 g) were added and the mixture was stirred for the appropriate time
(see Table 1). After completion of the reaction (followed by TLC), the
catalyst was separated by filtration. The solvent was evaporated and the
reaction mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL) and H2O (15 mL). The
organic phase was separated, dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated under
vacuum, and the crude mixture was purified by column chromatography
(hexane-EtOAc, 8:2); this afforded the pure dimethyl phosphonate 4. 4k,
yield 89%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Coupling of aldehydes, amines, and trimethyl phosphite promoted by
Amberlyst-15: highly efficient synthesis of α-aminophosphonates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tajbakhsh, Mahmood; Heydari, Akbar; Alinezhad, Heshmatollah; Ghanei,
Mercedeh; Khaksar, Samad
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2008), (3), 352-354

