$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of PAP. PAP was synthesized through Kabachnik-Fields reaction
(Scheme 1).32,33 The preparation procedure was as follows: terephthalic
aldehyde (5.00 g, 0.037 mol), DETA (3.85 g, 0.037 mol), and diethyl
phosphonate (30 mL) were placed in a 100 mL round-bottomed flask with a
condenser on it. After being continuously stirred at 120°C for 24 h under
an argon atmosphere, the viscous orange-yellow transparent product was
dissolved in ethanol and light-yellow powder was then obtained by
precipitating the above solution in anhydrous ether. This
dissolve-precipitate process was repeated for three times to remove the
unreacted terephthalic aldehyde, diethylenetriamine, and diethyl
phosphonate. Finally, PAP of 16.45 g was obtained. The yield was 86%. Mn
: 3100 g.mol-1, Mw : 4500 g.mol-1, D: 1.45.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM polymerization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Polymer Containing α-Aminophosphonate Unit Used as Reactive,
Halogen-Free Flame Retardant for Epoxy Resins
