$DATUM 67-68-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of poly(4-vinyl benzaldehyde) (poly(St-CHO)). A DMSO solution
(40 mL) of St-CHO (10.0 g, 76 mmol) and AIBN (128 mg, 0.76 mmol) was
degassed with Ar at r.t. for 10 minutes. After degassing, the reaction
mixture was stirred at 80 °C overnight. The reaction mixture was exposed
in air to quench the polymerization. The polymer was purified by
re-precipitation (CHCl3/MeOH). White powder, yield 7.77 g (77.7 %). SEC
(DMF); Mn = 42,000, PDI = 2.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM polymer post treated with different phosphites and amines, aerobic (stage
2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Multicomponent Postpolymerization Modification Based on
Kabachnik-Fields Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kakuchi, Ryohei; Theato, Patrick
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM ACS Macro Letters (2014), 3(4), 329-332

