$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 6a-6f by reaction of 7a, 7b with
dialkyl phosphites 4a-4c. A mixture of 0.8 g of the Schiff bases 7a, 7b
(2.2 mmol) and dimethyl (4a), diethyl (4b), or diisopropyl phosphite (4c)
(2.5 mmol) in 15 cm3 THF containing 10 % FeCl3 was heated under reflux
for 10-15 h (TLC). After the usual working up, as it is described in the
general procedure, and crystallization from the proper solvent,
phosphonates 6a-6f were isolated. After completion of the reaction (the
evolved H2 gas was observed but not tested), 10 cm3 AcOEt was added to
the mixture. The organic phase was separated, washed with 20 cm3
distilled H2O, and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Solvents were evaporated
under reduced pressure, and the residue therein was crystallized from the
proper solvent. Diethyl
5,7-di-tert-butyl-2-(4-fluorophenyl)-2,3-dihydrobenzo[d]oxazol-2-ylphosphonate
(6b, C25H35FNO4P) Colorless crystals; 795 mg (78 %). m.p.: 114 °C
(pentane); IR (KBr): ν = 3,345w (NH), 1,245 (P═O), 1,125 (P-O-C) cm-1; 1H
NMR (500.7 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.29 (dt, JH-H = 6.6 Hz, 4JP-H = 4.8 Hz, 6H,
(MeCO)2P), 1.37, 1.44 [2 s, 2 × 9H, 2(Me3C)], 4.22 (dq, JH-H = 6.6, 3JP-H
= 5.7 Hz, 4H, (H2CO)2P), 6.35 (d, JH-H = 4.2 Hz, 1H, H(4)-Ar), 6.96 (d,
JH-H = 4.2 Hz, 1H, H(6)-Ar), 7.36, 7.82 (2 m, 4H, H-Ar), 8.91 (br s, 1H,
HN) ppm; 13C NMR (125.4 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 163.9, 149.2, 148.6, 134.0,
132.3, 128.2, 119.4, 117.5, 116.4, 112.2 (C-Ar), 90.2 (d, 1JP-C = 136 Hz,
C-P), 63.2 (d, 2JP-C = 14.8 Hz, (CH2O)2P), 38.7, 30.5 (2CMe3), 31.2, 29.4
(2Me3C), 16.2 (d, 3JP-C = 7.8 Hz, MeCOP) ppm; 31P NMR (200.7 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 27.9 ppm; MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 462 (23) [M+ -1], 442 (53) [M+
-20, (H + F)], 305 (100) [M+ -157, (H + F + P(O)(OEt)2)], 191 (90), 138
(62) [P(O)(OEt)2)], 77 (78).
