$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of
α-Aminophosphonates Aromatic aldehyde (1 mmol), amine (1 mmol), and
trimethyl phosphite (1 mmol) were mixed with well-dispersed GO (3 mg) in
methanol and stirred at room temperature except for diamine (entry 11k,
Table 3), where the molar amount of carbonyl compound and phosphite was
twice as much as the amine. The progress of the reaction was monitored by
thin-layer chromatography (TLC) using a solvent system consisting of a
mixture of hexane and ethyl acetate (7:3). After completion, the catalyst
was separated from the reaction mass by decantation. The reaction mass
was then quenched with 5% NaHCO3 solution (3 mL). Crude product was
extracted with dichloromethane (5 mL × 3). The organic layer was again
washed with 5% brine (3 mL) solution and dried over sodium sulfate for an
appropriate time. The crude product was analyzed without further
purification using various analytical techniques such as mass
spectrometry (MS), 1H NMR, 13C NMR, IR, and elemental analysis
techniques. Compound 6f: White Solid. MF = C14H22NO3P, mp: 109ºC; [3] IR
(KBr): ν max 3322 (-NH), 2948 (-CH), 1240 (-P=O), 1183 (P-O-Me), 1030
(P-O-Me) out of phase, 754 (P-O-Me) in phase; 1H NMR(200MHz,CDCl3,TMS): δ
= δ 1.22-1.93 (m, 8H), 2.16-2.26 (Br, 2H), 3.68 (s, 3H), 3.70 (s, 3H),
6.78-6.85 (t, J = 14 Hz, 1H), 7.01-7.04 (d, J = 6 Hz, 2H), 7.14-7.22 (t,
J = 16 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR(50MHz,CDCl3,TMS): δ = 19.86 (-CH2), 25.11 (-CH2),
30.32 (-CH2), 53.02 (OCH3), 118.43 (CH), 119.57 (CH), 128.86 (CH).
Analytically calculated for C14H22NO3P: C, 59.36; H, 7.81; N, 4.94; Found
C, 59.53; H, 7.79; N, 4.92. MS (ESI): m/z [M + K]+ = 322.04.
